WEBVTT

00:00:12.012 --> 00:00:13.639
Beautiful, isn't it?

00:00:13.713 --> 00:00:15.180
A sensor analysis

00:00:15.248 --> 00:00:17.944
would have provided
the necessary information.

00:00:18.018 --> 00:00:19.508
Just admiring the view.

00:00:19.586 --> 00:00:21.952
The conference begins
in less than an hour.

00:00:22.022 --> 00:00:24.081
There's always time
for warp field dynamics,

00:00:24.157 --> 00:00:26.990
but you don't see natural
beauty like this every day.

00:00:28.728 --> 00:00:30.389
What was that?

00:00:30.463 --> 00:00:32.954
Some kind of energy barrier
directly below us.

00:00:33.099 --> 00:00:35.727
It spans thousands
of square kilometers.

00:00:35.802 --> 00:00:37.201
Why didn't our sensors
detect it?

00:00:37.270 --> 00:00:38.362
I'm not certain.

00:00:38.438 --> 00:00:40.633
It has an unusual
tetryon signature.

00:00:40.707 --> 00:00:44.575
Species 312 used a
similar technology.

00:00:47.847 --> 00:00:50.816
There's a power surge
coming from the barrier.

00:00:50.884 --> 00:00:52.875
Shields at full.

00:00:54.421 --> 00:00:56.355
They're creating
some kind of feedback.

00:00:56.423 --> 00:00:58.357
We've lost impulse engines.

00:00:58.425 --> 00:00:59.119
Go to warp.

00:01:00.627 --> 00:01:02.390
The warp core is off-line.

00:01:02.462 --> 00:01:04.054
Warp engines
don't just shut down

00:01:04.130 --> 00:01:05.757
when you scrape
an energy barrier.

00:01:05.832 --> 00:01:07.527
It's affecting all our systems.

00:01:07.600 --> 00:01:08.532
Warning.

00:01:08.601 --> 00:01:10.034
Structural failure
in 30 seconds.

00:01:10.103 --> 00:01:11.593
We'll have to beam
to the surface.

00:01:11.671 --> 00:01:13.901
We can't transport
through the barrier.

00:01:13.973 --> 00:01:16.168
Transfer auxiliary power
to the weapons array.

00:01:16.242 --> 00:01:17.470
What are you trying to do?

00:01:17.544 --> 00:01:19.273
If I can realign our phasers
to the correct

00:01:19.345 --> 00:01:21.279
frequency, I may be
able to open a rift.

00:01:21.347 --> 00:01:23.178
Big enough to get
a shuttle through, I hope.

00:01:23.249 --> 00:01:26.184
Warning. Structural failure
in ten seconds...

00:01:26.252 --> 00:01:28.652
nine... eight...

00:01:28.721 --> 00:01:30.188
Phasers reconfigured.

00:01:30.256 --> 00:01:31.314
...five...

00:03:37.650 --> 00:03:39.208
The barrier's closed again.

00:03:47.227 --> 00:03:48.888
I should examine you.

00:03:48.962 --> 00:03:51.157
I don't think it's serious.

00:04:05.945 --> 00:04:07.845
You have a hairline fracture.

00:04:07.914 --> 00:04:10.474
We've got bigger problems.
I'll be fine.

00:04:12.352 --> 00:04:14.047
I'm detecting
shuttle debris scattered

00:04:14.120 --> 00:04:16.213
over several square kilometers.

00:04:16.289 --> 00:04:17.517
Some of it
might still be functional.

00:04:17.590 --> 00:04:18.818
If we can find
the right components,

00:04:18.891 --> 00:04:19.823
we may be able

00:04:19.892 --> 00:04:22.452
to construct a beacon,
send a distress signal.

00:04:22.528 --> 00:04:24.826
Through the barrier?

00:04:26.566 --> 00:04:27.897
Maybe.

00:04:29.802 --> 00:04:33.568
If we hurry, we might
still make that conference.

00:04:33.640 --> 00:04:37.906
Well, if we have
to be stranded somewhere,

00:04:37.977 --> 00:04:40.275
you couldn't ask
for a nicer place.

00:04:40.346 --> 00:04:41.870
We wouldn't be
stranded at all

00:04:41.948 --> 00:04:44.974
if you hadn't insisted
on admiring the view.

00:04:56.162 --> 00:04:58.824
Guest Vessel 74656,

00:04:58.898 --> 00:05:00.195
this is Ledos Port Control.

00:05:00.266 --> 00:05:01.426
Shut down your engines.

00:05:01.501 --> 00:05:03.196
This is Lieutenant Tom Paris.

00:05:03.269 --> 00:05:04.736
Is there a problem?

00:05:04.804 --> 00:05:07.602
You were observed committing
Piloting Violation 256.

00:05:07.674 --> 00:05:11.007
I'm sorry, I'm not familiar
with your regulations.

00:05:11.077 --> 00:05:12.544
It won't happen again.

00:05:12.612 --> 00:05:14.910
You will be informed
of the penalty.

00:05:14.981 --> 00:05:16.915
What kind of "penalty"?

00:05:16.983 --> 00:05:18.450
That's not my decision.

00:05:18.518 --> 00:05:20.486
Your docking permit
says you're assigned

00:05:20.553 --> 00:05:22.214
to the Starship Voyager.

00:05:22.288 --> 00:05:24.153
That's right.

00:05:24.223 --> 00:05:25.212
Your commanding officer

00:05:25.291 --> 00:05:28.624
will be notified
of your infraction.

00:05:28.695 --> 00:05:29.821
Piloting lessons?

00:05:29.896 --> 00:05:31.158
Well, apparently,

00:05:31.230 --> 00:05:33.027
the standard penalty
for your infraction

00:05:33.099 --> 00:05:34.862
is a three-day course
in flight safety

00:05:34.934 --> 00:05:36.265
followed by a test.

00:05:36.336 --> 00:05:37.701
Well, did you explain to them

00:05:37.770 --> 00:05:39.203
that we wouldn't be here
that long?

00:05:39.272 --> 00:05:41.297
Well, actually, while you were
completing your mission,

00:05:41.374 --> 00:05:42.864
Seven was invited
to a four-day conference.

00:05:42.942 --> 00:05:45.137
Here on Ledos?

00:05:45.211 --> 00:05:46.200
I decided to give

00:05:46.279 --> 00:05:47.507
the entire crew shore leave.

00:05:47.580 --> 00:05:48.877
It'll give you plenty of time

00:05:48.948 --> 00:05:50.540
to brush up
on your piloting skills.

00:05:50.616 --> 00:05:52.777
I don't need lessons.

00:05:52.852 --> 00:05:55.252
Apparently,
the authorities disagree.

00:05:55.321 --> 00:05:57.118
But, Captain...

00:05:57.190 --> 00:05:58.418
You may not have known

00:05:58.491 --> 00:06:00.891
the Ledosians' rules,
but you know ours.

00:06:00.960 --> 00:06:03.121
Comply with local law,
understood?

00:06:03.196 --> 00:06:06.222
Yes, ma'am.

00:06:21.280 --> 00:06:22.770
The relays are fused.

00:06:22.849 --> 00:06:24.817
It's useless.

00:06:28.654 --> 00:06:31.817
Looks like we're not
the only ones here.

00:06:31.891 --> 00:06:34.189
Indigenous wildlife, perhaps.

00:06:34.260 --> 00:06:37.195
I'm reading
residual life signs.

00:06:37.263 --> 00:06:38.855
They're humanoid.

00:06:38.931 --> 00:06:40.159
Ledosian?

00:06:40.233 --> 00:06:44.829
No, but they share the
same genetic traits.

00:06:44.904 --> 00:06:47.065
Whoever they are, they
may be able to help us.

00:06:47.140 --> 00:06:48.937
Unless they're hostile.

00:06:49.041 --> 00:06:52.841
Why don't we give them
the benefit of the doubt?

00:06:52.912 --> 00:06:54.937
The life signs lead
in that direction.

00:06:55.014 --> 00:06:58.040
I suggest you rest your leg
while I investigate.

00:06:58.117 --> 00:07:00.585
It's better if we
stick together.

00:07:00.653 --> 00:07:03.349
At least until we know
whether they're hostile.

00:07:21.274 --> 00:07:23.469
I'm guessing they're pre-warp.

00:07:23.543 --> 00:07:25.875
Obviously, they can't help us.

00:07:25.945 --> 00:07:30.211
No... I don't
suppose they can.

00:07:30.283 --> 00:07:32.046
But they're fascinating,
aren't they?

00:07:32.118 --> 00:07:35.349
I never expected
to run into people like these

00:07:35.421 --> 00:07:37.116
on such a technologically
advanced planet.

00:07:37.190 --> 00:07:40.682
This isn't an anthropological
mission, Commander.

00:07:40.760 --> 00:07:42.853
You're right.

00:07:42.929 --> 00:07:44.897
We should keep
searching for debris...

00:07:52.405 --> 00:07:55.374
You're developing an infection.

00:07:55.441 --> 00:07:57.432
You should rest.

00:07:57.510 --> 00:07:58.477
I'll have to stay here

00:07:58.544 --> 00:07:59.943
and try to keep out of sight.

00:08:00.012 --> 00:08:03.311
I'll contact you
if I find anything useful.

00:08:03.382 --> 00:08:05.782
I guess I don't
have to tell you

00:08:05.852 --> 00:08:08.844
to avoid interacting
with these people.

00:08:52.765 --> 00:08:54.960
Seven of Nine to Chakotay.

00:08:56.636 --> 00:08:58.968
Seven of Nine to Chakotay.

00:09:05.545 --> 00:09:07.479
Commander, respond.
I found something.

00:09:09.482 --> 00:09:10.779
Seven of Nine to Chakotay.

00:09:10.850 --> 00:09:12.147
Don't!

00:10:06.439 --> 00:10:07.531
Step away from him.

00:10:10.710 --> 00:10:12.644
It's all right, Seven.

00:10:12.712 --> 00:10:14.179
They're friendly.

00:10:14.246 --> 00:10:16.714
They're treating my wound.

00:10:27.927 --> 00:10:31.294
You said we were supposed
to avoid interaction.

00:10:31.364 --> 00:10:33.559
They found me. There
was nothing I could do.

00:10:33.633 --> 00:10:34.827
You should have tried
to contact me.

00:10:34.900 --> 00:10:37.528
I didn't want to expose
them to our technology.

00:10:39.005 --> 00:10:40.973
You hid your combadge?

00:10:41.107 --> 00:10:43.166
Actually, your call scared them.

00:10:43.242 --> 00:10:44.436
They broke it.

00:10:44.510 --> 00:10:47.206
I suggest we leave
before they break anything else.

00:10:47.279 --> 00:10:49.839
Look, they're friendly...

00:10:49.915 --> 00:10:51.177
and I am hurt.

00:10:51.250 --> 00:10:53.218
What are you suggesting?

00:10:53.285 --> 00:10:54.752
We may as well stay the night.

00:10:54.820 --> 00:10:55.878
Commander...

00:10:55.955 --> 00:10:56.979
It's good shelter,

00:10:57.089 --> 00:10:59.353
and my leg feels better
since they put

00:10:59.425 --> 00:11:00.449
this dressing on.

00:11:00.526 --> 00:11:03.393
I'm going to get some rest.

00:11:03.462 --> 00:11:05.862
I suggest you do the same.

00:11:49.975 --> 00:11:52.535
Chell says we shouldn't
miss the flame gardens.

00:11:52.611 --> 00:11:54.772
I hear the arboretum
is beautiful, too.

00:11:54.847 --> 00:11:55.871
We can do both.

00:11:55.948 --> 00:11:56.972
Tom!

00:11:57.049 --> 00:11:57.981
You joining us?

00:11:58.050 --> 00:11:58.982
Oh, that's right.

00:11:59.051 --> 00:12:00.382
You have to go to pilot school.

00:12:01.587 --> 00:12:02.884
I hear the course takes days.

00:12:02.955 --> 00:12:03.922
Yeah, for most people,

00:12:04.056 --> 00:12:05.455
but I did a little research.

00:12:05.524 --> 00:12:07.890
If the instructor agrees,
you can skip the lessons

00:12:07.960 --> 00:12:09.291
and go right to the test.

00:12:09.361 --> 00:12:11.556
So, I will be seeing you
in a couple of hours.

00:12:11.630 --> 00:12:14.599
You have to admire his optimism.

00:12:14.667 --> 00:12:16.635
Just a moment, sir.

00:12:23.709 --> 00:12:27.201
I am Mr. Kleg,
the flying instructor.

00:12:27.279 --> 00:12:29.076
Are you Lieutenant Paris?

00:12:29.148 --> 00:12:30.740
He is.

00:12:30.816 --> 00:12:32.716
It's an honor to meet you, sir.

00:12:32.785 --> 00:12:34.412
May I show you
to the Delta Flyer?

00:12:34.487 --> 00:12:35.818
Why?

00:12:35.888 --> 00:12:38.550
So you can explain
what I did wrong

00:12:38.624 --> 00:12:40.285
and then administer the test.

00:12:40.359 --> 00:12:41.519
It sounds to me

00:12:41.594 --> 00:12:44.290
like you need lessons
in patience, as well.

00:12:44.363 --> 00:12:45.295
Oh, Tom is

00:12:45.364 --> 00:12:47.161
very patient, sir.

00:12:47.233 --> 00:12:49.098
Never impulsive.

00:12:49.168 --> 00:12:51.602
Take all the time you need.

00:12:51.670 --> 00:12:53.501
He'll enjoy
the extra attention.

00:12:53.572 --> 00:12:55.437
Well, I'm pleased to hear it.

00:12:55.508 --> 00:12:58.272
We'll start with a review
of safety procedures.

00:12:58.344 --> 00:12:59.276
Do you have a visual

00:12:59.345 --> 00:13:01.905
display system I can access?

00:13:01.981 --> 00:13:03.881
I think I can find one.

00:13:03.949 --> 00:13:04.813
Have fun.

00:13:06.385 --> 00:13:09.548
Energize.

00:13:11.423 --> 00:13:13.823
So, how long will
this "review" take?

00:13:13.893 --> 00:13:17.420
Oh, typically
about four hours,

00:13:17.496 --> 00:13:18.554
but there's no rush.

00:13:20.432 --> 00:13:21.399
Of course not.

00:13:33.245 --> 00:13:35.372
River.

00:13:44.723 --> 00:13:46.315
River.

00:13:55.134 --> 00:13:57.034
Mountain.

00:14:01.473 --> 00:14:03.600
Mountain.

00:14:09.048 --> 00:14:11.744
Where... are we?

00:14:26.165 --> 00:14:27.359
This?

00:14:36.508 --> 00:14:40.376
You want to trade.

00:14:40.446 --> 00:14:43.415
Well, I suppose it won't hurt.

00:14:51.457 --> 00:14:53.652
I'll take that as a "thank you."

00:15:01.200 --> 00:15:03.464
Did you make
a favorable exchange?

00:15:03.535 --> 00:15:05.696
I didn't want to
insult their customs.

00:15:05.771 --> 00:15:06.863
Any luck?

00:15:06.939 --> 00:15:08.907
I may have found a way
of communicating.

00:15:09.008 --> 00:15:10.669
Me, too.

00:15:10.743 --> 00:15:12.233
I've learned how
to say "thank you."

00:15:12.311 --> 00:15:13.676
I was referring

00:15:13.746 --> 00:15:15.008
to communication
with Voyager.

00:15:15.080 --> 00:15:16.809
It may be possible
to construct a beacon

00:15:16.882 --> 00:15:18.213
by connecting
these components

00:15:18.284 --> 00:15:19.478
to the shuttle's deflector.

00:15:19.551 --> 00:15:20.609
Did you find it?

00:15:20.686 --> 00:15:22.517
I detected it
six kilometers from here.

00:15:22.588 --> 00:15:23.850
I believe it's intact.

00:15:23.923 --> 00:15:26.289
I'm not sure I'm up
to that long a trip.

00:15:26.358 --> 00:15:29.122
I'll go.

00:15:29.194 --> 00:15:31.219
I've started mapping the area.

00:15:31.297 --> 00:15:33.390
Here's the river we passed.

00:15:33.465 --> 00:15:34.659
This is where we beamed down

00:15:34.733 --> 00:15:36.325
and we're here now.

00:15:36.402 --> 00:15:39.803
Then the deflector should
be approximately here.

00:15:39.872 --> 00:15:42.340
Six kilometers is a long way.

00:15:42.408 --> 00:15:44.308
Maybe one of them
could guide you.

00:15:44.376 --> 00:15:45.400
I'm still trying

00:15:45.477 --> 00:15:47.468
to limit our contact
with these people.

00:15:47.546 --> 00:15:49.343
The sooner we get
to the deflector,

00:15:49.415 --> 00:15:51.542
the sooner we can
get out of here.

00:15:51.617 --> 00:15:52.811
They know the terrain.

00:15:52.885 --> 00:15:54.512
Maybe they can
get you there faster.

00:15:54.586 --> 00:15:55.678
And watch me construct

00:15:55.754 --> 00:15:57.483
a tetryon-based
signaling device?

00:15:59.625 --> 00:16:01.684
All right, but be careful.

00:16:06.799 --> 00:16:08.198
Seven.

00:16:08.267 --> 00:16:12.067
This is how they say "good-bye."

00:17:15.534 --> 00:17:17.001
Thank you.

00:17:27.646 --> 00:17:28.613
Hello.

00:18:26.638 --> 00:18:29.163
Identify yourself.

00:19:20.425 --> 00:19:24.054
An exothermic reaction.

00:19:48.687 --> 00:19:50.882
I'm not hungry.

00:20:03.835 --> 00:20:06.770
Inadequate system integration.

00:20:06.838 --> 00:20:11.832
Visibility impaired
by lateral sensor array.

00:20:11.910 --> 00:20:15.471
Insufficient console
accessibility...

00:20:15.547 --> 00:20:17.139
You know, I
couldn't agree more.

00:20:17.216 --> 00:20:18.945
Those are just
some of the defects

00:20:19.051 --> 00:20:21.110
that led to my so-
called "pilot error."

00:20:21.186 --> 00:20:22.517
Polarity thrusters?

00:20:22.588 --> 00:20:27.753
Oh! They've been known to cause
accidental acceleration.

00:20:27.826 --> 00:20:29.293
Exactly my point.

00:20:29.361 --> 00:20:32.489
Why should I be held responsible
for the ship's design flaws?

00:20:32.564 --> 00:20:35.931
According
to the maintenance records,

00:20:36.001 --> 00:20:38.333
you were this vessel's
chief designer.

00:20:38.403 --> 00:20:40.701
I make it a point
of professional pride

00:20:40.772 --> 00:20:42.967
to research every case
I'm assigned to.

00:20:43.041 --> 00:20:45.532
Are you familiar with that term,
Lieutenant?

00:20:45.611 --> 00:20:47.511
Professional pride?

00:20:47.579 --> 00:20:48.705
Yes, sir.

00:20:49.615 --> 00:20:51.139
In fact, that is why

00:20:51.216 --> 00:20:53.116
I am so eager to get underway.

00:20:53.185 --> 00:20:56.245
I want to prove to you
that I am a good pilot.

00:20:56.321 --> 00:20:58.949
There are protocols, Mr. Paris.

00:20:59.024 --> 00:21:01.959
System by system diagnostics,
preflight simulations...

00:21:02.027 --> 00:21:04.928
You must have other students
who need your attention.

00:21:04.997 --> 00:21:06.692
It wouldn't be fair to...

00:21:06.765 --> 00:21:08.926
Don't worry, Lieutenant.

00:21:09.067 --> 00:21:13.231
I'm planning to spend as much
time with you as you need.

00:21:30.656 --> 00:21:32.988
Good morning.

00:22:03.488 --> 00:22:05.513
I'm trying to go here.

00:22:18.537 --> 00:22:20.027
Can you show me?

00:22:51.036 --> 00:22:52.503
Yes.

00:22:55.307 --> 00:22:57.275
I thought it was this way.

00:23:17.662 --> 00:23:19.926
Yes, it's quite
an impressive view,

00:23:19.998 --> 00:23:21.795
but now we really have...

00:23:52.364 --> 00:23:54.093
My friend...

00:23:55.967 --> 00:23:58.265
She hasn't come back.

00:23:58.336 --> 00:24:00.497
I need to find her.

00:24:12.083 --> 00:24:14.677
She looks like this.

00:24:16.288 --> 00:24:18.381
Where?

00:24:29.401 --> 00:24:31.198
Where did you get this?

00:24:55.460 --> 00:24:58.554
My friend.

00:24:58.630 --> 00:25:00.188
Where?

00:25:19.184 --> 00:25:19.980
Don't touch that!

00:25:22.187 --> 00:25:23.119
Please.

00:25:42.674 --> 00:25:44.266
Problem?

00:25:44.342 --> 00:25:46.139
Commander Chakotay
failed to report in

00:25:46.211 --> 00:25:47.269
at the scheduled time.

00:25:47.345 --> 00:25:49.472
We tried hailing,
but there was no response.

00:25:49.548 --> 00:25:51.448
We contacted
the conference coordinator.

00:25:51.516 --> 00:25:53.541
He said Seven and Chakotay
never showed up.

00:25:53.618 --> 00:25:55.210
Anything on sensors?

00:25:55.287 --> 00:25:56.515
We located
a hull signature

00:25:56.588 --> 00:25:57.953
over the southern
subcontinent,

00:25:58.089 --> 00:26:00.922
but it's only a wing.

00:26:00.992 --> 00:26:03.051
Nothing else? No life signs?

00:26:03.128 --> 00:26:04.891
No, ma'am.

00:26:04.963 --> 00:26:07.761
That's awfully low
for something to be in orbit.

00:26:07.832 --> 00:26:09.129
It's not in orbit.

00:26:09.200 --> 00:26:12.101
It's resting on
an energy barrier.

00:26:12.170 --> 00:26:14.832
We think the shuttle may
have collided with it.

00:26:14.906 --> 00:26:16.203
Why didn't they see it?

00:26:16.274 --> 00:26:18.037
Standard scans
didn't reveal its presence.

00:26:18.109 --> 00:26:20.373
We were only able to detect it
with our Borg sensors.

00:26:20.445 --> 00:26:21.844
If all you found was a wing,

00:26:21.913 --> 00:26:24.143
maybe the rest of the shuttle
made it through the barrier.

00:26:24.215 --> 00:26:26.046
Logic suggests that possibility.

00:26:26.117 --> 00:26:28.677
Unfortunately, the barrier
is deflecting all our scans.

00:26:28.753 --> 00:26:30.380
There's no way to know

00:26:30.455 --> 00:26:33.049
if the shuttle or its occupants
are on the other side.

00:26:33.124 --> 00:26:36.651
Hail the Ledosian Ambassador.

00:26:38.296 --> 00:26:39.695
We'd have warned your Commander,

00:26:39.764 --> 00:26:41.823
but his flight plan didn't go
anywhere near that area.

00:26:41.900 --> 00:26:44.368
He must have altered his route
for some reason.

00:26:44.436 --> 00:26:46.336
And collided with the barrier.

00:26:46.404 --> 00:26:47.632
I'm sorry.

00:26:47.706 --> 00:26:49.674
We're not assuming they're dead.

00:26:49.741 --> 00:26:52.141
We believe they may
have found a way through.

00:26:52.210 --> 00:26:53.507
That's very unlikely.

00:26:53.578 --> 00:26:55.512
They're resourceful people.

00:26:55.580 --> 00:26:57.741
Can you tell us anything
about the barrier?

00:26:57.816 --> 00:27:00.250
It shields the territory
of an indigenous society...

00:27:00.318 --> 00:27:01.751
the Ventu.

00:27:01.820 --> 00:27:03.378
Then the area's habitable.

00:27:03.455 --> 00:27:05.047
If you lowered the barrier,

00:27:05.123 --> 00:27:07.318
we could scan
for our people's life signs.

00:27:07.392 --> 00:27:09.519
I'm afraid we can't do that.

00:27:09.594 --> 00:27:10.686
Why not?

00:27:10.762 --> 00:27:12.662
It was erected by aliens

00:27:12.731 --> 00:27:14.426
hundreds of years ago.

00:27:14.499 --> 00:27:16.262
They haven't been back.

00:27:16.334 --> 00:27:18.894
The technology
is a mystery to us.

00:27:18.970 --> 00:27:21.495
Why did these aliens
build the barrier?

00:27:21.573 --> 00:27:23.234
To protect the Ventu.

00:27:23.308 --> 00:27:24.707
From whom?

00:27:24.776 --> 00:27:26.243
Us.

00:27:26.311 --> 00:27:28.905
Our ancestors fought them,
polluted their habitat.

00:27:29.014 --> 00:27:32.450
I'm afraid we weren't
very enlightened back then.

00:27:32.517 --> 00:27:35.350
Earth went through its dark
periods too, Ambassador.

00:27:35.420 --> 00:27:38.821
Would you have any objections
if we tried to lower the barrier

00:27:38.890 --> 00:27:40.721
just to scan for our people?

00:27:40.792 --> 00:27:42.521
I told you, it's not possible.

00:27:42.594 --> 00:27:44.255
Perhaps if you
gave us information

00:27:44.329 --> 00:27:45.921
about the barrier's
power source.

00:27:46.031 --> 00:27:47.589
The generator is inside.

00:27:47.666 --> 00:27:49.566
There's no way to access it.

00:27:49.634 --> 00:27:52.933
Even if your people did survive,

00:27:53.004 --> 00:27:56.098
I'm afraid
there's no way to get them out.

00:28:01.846 --> 00:28:06.146
Captain's Log, Stardate 54827.7.

00:28:06.217 --> 00:28:07.980
Although the Ledosians
are skeptical,

00:28:08.053 --> 00:28:10.419
they're allowing us
to try to locate our people.

00:28:10.488 --> 00:28:11.614
Meanwhile, we've begun

00:28:11.690 --> 00:28:13.419
to analyze
the shuttle fragment.

00:28:13.491 --> 00:28:15.083
The burn pattern suggests

00:28:15.160 --> 00:28:16.422
a tetryon flux.

00:28:16.494 --> 00:28:18.758
We found a reference
to similar technology

00:28:18.830 --> 00:28:20.593
in Seven's Borg database.

00:28:20.665 --> 00:28:22.656
You think the Borg erected it?

00:28:22.734 --> 00:28:25.897
No, but it may have been
constructed by people

00:28:26.004 --> 00:28:28.905
they later assimilated...
Species 312.

00:28:29.007 --> 00:28:31.498
If Seven were here,
she might be able to figure out

00:28:31.576 --> 00:28:32.770
a way to get through it.

00:28:32.844 --> 00:28:34.778
Maybe she already did.

00:28:34.846 --> 00:28:36.711
Some of the damage to
the wing was caused

00:28:36.781 --> 00:28:38.612
by feedback from the
shuttle's phasers.

00:28:38.683 --> 00:28:40.708
Seven and Chakotay
might have used them

00:28:40.785 --> 00:28:42.912
to penetrate the barrier
for some reason.

00:28:43.021 --> 00:28:44.511
If I can determine

00:28:44.589 --> 00:28:45.749
the appropriate frequency,

00:28:45.824 --> 00:28:47.451
I may be able
to do the same thing.

00:28:47.525 --> 00:28:48.719
But there is risk involved.

00:28:48.793 --> 00:28:50.055
What sort of risk?

00:28:50.128 --> 00:28:51.925
It looks like
the feedback from the barrier

00:28:51.996 --> 00:28:53.224
is what destroyed the shuttle.

00:28:53.298 --> 00:28:54.390
If we're not careful,

00:28:54.466 --> 00:28:56.457
the same thing could
happen to Voyager.

00:29:25.430 --> 00:29:27.057
May I see those?

00:29:35.173 --> 00:29:36.435
Seven.

00:29:36.508 --> 00:29:38.100
Is everything all right?

00:29:38.176 --> 00:29:40.144
I need your tricorder.

00:29:43.348 --> 00:29:44.610
Nice to see you, too.

00:29:44.682 --> 00:29:48.118
I lost mine.

00:29:48.186 --> 00:29:50.245
There's a strong
magnetic field here

00:29:50.321 --> 00:29:53.449
that's preventing me from
generating a deflector beam,

00:29:53.525 --> 00:29:55.254
but the field drops off

00:29:55.326 --> 00:29:59.626
approximately 4.8 kilometers
in that direction.

00:29:59.697 --> 00:30:01.631
Can you transmit the
signal from there?

00:30:01.699 --> 00:30:02.859
Not through the barrier,

00:30:02.934 --> 00:30:04.265
but I may be able
to neutralize it

00:30:04.335 --> 00:30:06.394
by generating a dampening field
with our deflector.

00:30:06.471 --> 00:30:10.805
Even if you're right,
this must weigh 500 kilos.

00:30:10.875 --> 00:30:12.240
How would we move it?

00:30:15.180 --> 00:30:16.647
Some of them could help us.

00:30:16.714 --> 00:30:18.113
We shouldn't involve them.

00:30:18.183 --> 00:30:20.481
Do I detect a change
in attitude, Commander?

00:30:24.055 --> 00:30:25.317
Your concern was justified.

00:30:25.390 --> 00:30:27.483
They've been gathering
debris from the shuttle,

00:30:27.559 --> 00:30:28.821
using it to imitate us.

00:30:28.893 --> 00:30:30.451
I don't want them helping.

00:30:30.528 --> 00:30:31.825
What's the alternative?

00:30:31.896 --> 00:30:33.158
Staying here?

00:30:33.231 --> 00:30:35.165
Allowing them to find
all of the debris?

00:30:35.233 --> 00:30:36.723
If we neutralize the barrier,

00:30:36.801 --> 00:30:38.735
Voyager can transport us
and our technology

00:30:38.803 --> 00:30:39.963
off the surface.

00:30:40.038 --> 00:30:42.666
Is there a possibility
that this dampening field

00:30:42.740 --> 00:30:44.833
could disrupt the
barrier permanently?

00:30:44.909 --> 00:30:45.898
Unlikely.

00:30:45.977 --> 00:30:47.444
Once the deflector
is deactivated,

00:30:47.512 --> 00:30:48.979
the barrier should reinitialize.

00:30:49.047 --> 00:30:51.311
Let's hope you're right.

00:30:56.387 --> 00:30:58.912
So, you can execute a turn

00:30:58.990 --> 00:31:00.787
at less than 300 KPH.

00:31:00.859 --> 00:31:02.292
Well done, Lieutenant.

00:31:02.360 --> 00:31:03.793
Thanks.

00:31:03.862 --> 00:31:06.558
You know, I don't want
to seem impatient again,

00:31:06.631 --> 00:31:07.791
but is there any way

00:31:07.866 --> 00:31:09.800
that you'd let me
take that test now?

00:31:09.868 --> 00:31:12.098
I thought I made myself clear
about that.

00:31:12.170 --> 00:31:13.262
All my students

00:31:13.338 --> 00:31:15.465
complete the entire course.

00:31:15.540 --> 00:31:17.098
Well, I understand, sir,

00:31:17.175 --> 00:31:19.405
but two of my friends
are missing,

00:31:19.477 --> 00:31:21.672
and I'd like to help find them.

00:31:21.746 --> 00:31:23.213
Well, that's
an admirable sentiment,

00:31:23.281 --> 00:31:24.748
but if I give you
special treatment,

00:31:24.816 --> 00:31:26.215
it wouldn't be fair
to the others

00:31:26.284 --> 00:31:27.945
who have to take this course.

00:31:28.052 --> 00:31:29.280
Besides...

00:31:29.354 --> 00:31:30.946
why stop now?

00:31:31.055 --> 00:31:34.991
You're getting very close
to becoming an adequate pilot.

00:31:44.302 --> 00:31:46.702
Here, Commander.

00:31:57.849 --> 00:31:59.817
Not so close.

00:32:10.261 --> 00:32:12.889
Phasers are starting
to overload.

00:32:12.964 --> 00:32:14.829
Can we divert any more
power to the shields?

00:32:14.899 --> 00:32:17.766
The shields are amplifying
the feedback.

00:32:19.003 --> 00:32:20.334
The barrier's interfering

00:32:20.405 --> 00:32:22.066
with every system we activate.

00:32:22.140 --> 00:32:23.903
Cease fire.

00:32:25.910 --> 00:32:27.605
I'm open to suggestions.

00:32:27.679 --> 00:32:30.409
We may be able

00:32:30.481 --> 00:32:31.914
to reconfigure a photon torpedo

00:32:31.983 --> 00:32:33.917
to detonate
at the appropriate frequency.

00:32:33.985 --> 00:32:35.452
What about feedback?

00:32:35.520 --> 00:32:37.784
A torpedo
shouldn't create any...

00:32:37.855 --> 00:32:39.152
theoretically.

00:32:40.892 --> 00:32:42.223
Do it.

00:32:48.967 --> 00:32:51.868
They're too close.

00:32:55.506 --> 00:32:56.768
Back...

00:32:56.841 --> 00:32:58.775
behind the rise.

00:32:58.843 --> 00:33:00.208
Stay back.

00:33:20.698 --> 00:33:22.632
The energy barrier's
coming down.

00:33:22.700 --> 00:33:24.930
I thought you were
still reconfiguring

00:33:25.036 --> 00:33:25.934
the torpedo.

00:33:26.037 --> 00:33:27.129
I am.

00:33:27.205 --> 00:33:29.173
It's being deactivated
from the inside.

00:33:29.240 --> 00:33:30.764
Harry, scan for life signs.

00:33:30.842 --> 00:33:32.332
Aye, Captain.

00:33:39.417 --> 00:33:40.406
Take it off!

00:33:47.225 --> 00:33:49.159
I'm only reading one combadge.

00:33:49.227 --> 00:33:50.524
It's Seven's.

00:33:50.595 --> 00:33:51.687
Open a channel.

00:33:51.763 --> 00:33:52.855
Janeway to Seven.

00:33:52.930 --> 00:33:54.261
Are you and Chakotay all right?

00:33:54.332 --> 00:33:55.424
Yes, Captain.

00:33:55.500 --> 00:33:57.468
Stand by for transport.

00:33:57.535 --> 00:33:58.934
Lock on to Commander Chakotay.

00:33:59.003 --> 00:33:59.935
I need more time.

00:34:00.004 --> 00:34:00.936
Is there a problem?

00:34:01.005 --> 00:34:01.937
Someone's been injured.

00:34:02.006 --> 00:34:03.871
She requires
medical attention.

00:34:03.941 --> 00:34:05.033
Do you need the Doctor?

00:34:05.109 --> 00:34:06.201
I believe I can treat her.

00:34:06.277 --> 00:34:07.608
A medkit would be useful.

00:34:07.678 --> 00:34:09.646
Acknowledged.

00:34:10.715 --> 00:34:12.842
Captain's Log, supplemental.

00:34:12.917 --> 00:34:15.181
Seven has remained
on the surface

00:34:15.253 --> 00:34:17.551
to tend
to the injured Ventu girl

00:34:17.622 --> 00:34:20.648
while Chakotay's
being treated in Sick Bay.

00:34:22.193 --> 00:34:24.457
The poultice healed
the fracture and the infection.

00:34:24.529 --> 00:34:26.121
I'm impressed.

00:34:26.197 --> 00:34:27.789
They're impressive people.

00:34:27.865 --> 00:34:29.924
I just hope we haven't
traumatized them.

00:34:30.034 --> 00:34:32.468
You did what you had to do
to get out of there.

00:34:32.537 --> 00:34:33.936
Still, I think
we should transport

00:34:34.005 --> 00:34:35.632
all the shuttle debris
back to Voyager

00:34:35.706 --> 00:34:36.798
as soon as possible.

00:34:36.874 --> 00:34:38.543
Agreed.

00:34:43.648 --> 00:34:46.173
Would you like some breakfast?

00:34:49.720 --> 00:34:51.517
I'm not hungry, either.

00:35:00.331 --> 00:35:03.425
I admire your curiosity,

00:35:03.501 --> 00:35:05.662
but you should be more careful.

00:35:07.672 --> 00:35:09.572
It's time for me to leave.

00:35:14.479 --> 00:35:17.107
Back to my home.

00:35:24.622 --> 00:35:28.080
That's very kind,
but I have no use for it.

00:35:33.030 --> 00:35:36.488
I suppose I should respect
your customs.

00:35:37.268 --> 00:35:39.065
Thank you.

00:35:44.342 --> 00:35:46.276
These botanical specimens

00:35:46.344 --> 00:35:48.938
indicate a high level
of serum nitrates.

00:35:49.013 --> 00:35:51.038
Catalog those foliates.

00:35:51.115 --> 00:35:52.377
Explain your presence here.

00:35:52.450 --> 00:35:53.712
Oh.

00:35:53.784 --> 00:35:54.910
You must be from Voyager.

00:35:54.986 --> 00:35:55.918
Who are you?

00:35:55.987 --> 00:35:57.079
My name is Barus.

00:35:57.155 --> 00:35:58.247
I'm the expedition leader.

00:35:58.322 --> 00:36:00.256
What kind of expedition
are you leading?

00:36:00.324 --> 00:36:02.019
We're conducting
scans to evaluate

00:36:02.093 --> 00:36:03.560
the potential of this habitat.

00:36:03.628 --> 00:36:04.993
Potential for what?

00:36:05.062 --> 00:36:07.462
Anthropological research,
resource development...

00:36:07.532 --> 00:36:09.159
We've been waiting years
for this.

00:36:09.233 --> 00:36:11.565
What about the people
who live here?

00:36:11.636 --> 00:36:13.763
We'll help them, of course.

00:36:13.838 --> 00:36:15.237
How?

00:36:15.306 --> 00:36:16.398
With medicine,

00:36:16.474 --> 00:36:18.339
infrastructure, education...

00:36:18.409 --> 00:36:22.277
Whoever lowered this barrier
did the Ventu a great favor.

00:36:31.522 --> 00:36:33.114
That barrier has to go back up.

00:36:33.191 --> 00:36:34.385
Isn't it possible

00:36:34.458 --> 00:36:37.359
the Ledosians will improve
the lives of the Ventu?

00:36:37.428 --> 00:36:38.554
Lmprove them... how?

00:36:38.629 --> 00:36:40.221
They're intelligent people.

00:36:40.298 --> 00:36:42.732
Exposure to education
and technology

00:36:42.800 --> 00:36:44.427
may give them
better opportunities.

00:36:44.502 --> 00:36:45.434
Can you honestly say

00:36:45.503 --> 00:36:46.993
that you know
what's better for them?

00:36:49.240 --> 00:36:50.935
No, I can't.

00:36:51.075 --> 00:36:54.738
Then what do you think
we should do?

00:36:54.812 --> 00:36:56.780
I'm uncertain.

00:36:56.847 --> 00:36:59.407
It's not like you
to be on the fence.

00:37:00.818 --> 00:37:04.015
When Commander Chakotay and I
first encountered the Ventu,

00:37:04.088 --> 00:37:06.113
I found them primitive,
of little interest

00:37:06.190 --> 00:37:08.590
to me, but as I spent more
time with them, I came

00:37:08.659 --> 00:37:10.183
to realize that they're

00:37:10.261 --> 00:37:12.593
a resourceful,
self-reliant people.

00:37:12.663 --> 00:37:15.632
Their isolation may limit
their potential,

00:37:15.700 --> 00:37:17.793
but if that isolation ends,

00:37:17.868 --> 00:37:20.530
so will a unique way of life.

00:37:20.605 --> 00:37:22.698
We appreciate your help
in opening this territory

00:37:22.773 --> 00:37:24.468
to exploration, Captain.

00:37:24.542 --> 00:37:26.908
It's an unprecedented
opportunity.

00:37:26.978 --> 00:37:29.208
A short-lived opportunity,
I'm afraid.

00:37:29.280 --> 00:37:31.612
I don't understand.

00:37:31.682 --> 00:37:34.515
After I transport our
deflector back to Voyager,

00:37:34.585 --> 00:37:36.678
the energy barrier
will go back up.

00:37:36.754 --> 00:37:38.915
Naturally, you'll want
to get your people out,

00:37:38.990 --> 00:37:41.220
so they won't be trapped inside,
as ours were.

00:37:41.292 --> 00:37:44.125
You have no right to limit
our access to our own territory.

00:37:44.195 --> 00:37:46.789
I'm not trying to do that,
but we have a strict policy

00:37:46.864 --> 00:37:49.833
about leaving our technology
in the hands of other cultures.

00:37:49.900 --> 00:37:51.561
It often has
damaging consequences.

00:37:51.636 --> 00:37:53.831
I don't think you realize
how important it is.

00:37:53.904 --> 00:37:55.872
It's not only the resources
that interest us.

00:37:55.940 --> 00:37:58.374
The Ventu are
our evolutionary ancestors...

00:37:58.442 --> 00:38:01.309
our living history.

00:38:01.379 --> 00:38:03.370
I understand this is
disappointing for you,

00:38:03.447 --> 00:38:05.039
but I'm afraid I have no choice.

00:38:05.116 --> 00:38:09.644
In the spirit of cooperation,
I hope you'll reconsider.

00:38:09.720 --> 00:38:11.585
We're eager to resume course.

00:38:11.656 --> 00:38:15.592
Would an hour be enough time
for you to evacuate your people?

00:38:15.660 --> 00:38:18.390
I'll make the arrangements.

00:38:23.467 --> 00:38:25.094
We've transported
all the remaining debris

00:38:25.169 --> 00:38:26.329
to the cargo bay.

00:38:26.404 --> 00:38:28.770
I have a lock
on the deflector assembly.

00:38:28.839 --> 00:38:30.306
What is it?

00:38:30.374 --> 00:38:31.898
There's a Ledosian vessel

00:38:31.976 --> 00:38:33.136
on an intercept course.

00:38:33.210 --> 00:38:34.336
It's charging weapons.

00:38:34.412 --> 00:38:35.538
Shields.

00:38:39.116 --> 00:38:40.674
Direct hit to the transporters.

00:38:40.751 --> 00:38:41.775
They're off-line.

00:38:41.852 --> 00:38:43.717
Get a weapons lock
and hail them.

00:38:43.788 --> 00:38:45.449
They're hailing us.

00:38:45.523 --> 00:38:46.455
Captain Janeway.

00:38:46.524 --> 00:38:47.889
What's going on?

00:38:47.958 --> 00:38:49.084
Our government has decided

00:38:49.160 --> 00:38:50.718
not to let you
restore the barrier.

00:38:50.795 --> 00:38:53.389
And that justifies
an unprovoked attack?

00:38:53.464 --> 00:38:54.931
We only targeted
your transporters

00:38:55.032 --> 00:38:56.260
to avoid harming your crew.

00:38:56.334 --> 00:38:58.063
I hope you'll show
the same restraint.

00:38:58.135 --> 00:39:01.366
I don't find weapons fire
of any kind restrained.

00:39:01.439 --> 00:39:03.839
If you want to avoid
further conflict,

00:39:03.908 --> 00:39:05.205
I suggest you leave.

00:39:06.944 --> 00:39:08.138
Take us out of orbit.

00:39:08.212 --> 00:39:10.077
What about the deflector?

00:39:10.147 --> 00:39:12.138
Is Tom still in the Flyer?

00:39:12.216 --> 00:39:13.911
- Yes, ma'am.
- Hail him.

00:39:18.122 --> 00:39:19.589
Excellent, Mr. Paris.

00:39:19.657 --> 00:39:21.249
Now, come about slowly.

00:39:21.325 --> 00:39:23.088
Janeway to Paris. Respond.

00:39:23.160 --> 00:39:24.991
Captain, I would appreciate it

00:39:25.062 --> 00:39:27.257
if you wouldn't
interrupt my student

00:39:27.331 --> 00:39:28.798
during his examination.

00:39:28.866 --> 00:39:30.265
I'm sorry,
but something's come up.

00:39:30.334 --> 00:39:31.392
What is it, Captain?

00:39:31.469 --> 00:39:33.266
Tom, I'm sending you
some encrypted orders.

00:39:33.337 --> 00:39:34.668
Yes, ma'am.

00:39:34.739 --> 00:39:37.833
This is highly irregular.

00:39:44.815 --> 00:39:45.907
You're going much too fast!

00:39:45.983 --> 00:39:46.915
Yes, sir.

00:39:47.051 --> 00:39:48.780
I'm in a bit of a hurry.

00:39:48.853 --> 00:39:51.083
If you have any desire
to pass this test,

00:39:51.155 --> 00:39:53.248
you'll reduce your speed
immediately.

00:39:53.324 --> 00:39:54.586
I wish I could do that, sir.

00:39:54.658 --> 00:39:56.148
I really do.

00:39:59.764 --> 00:40:01.231
What was that?

00:40:01.298 --> 00:40:03.095
Paris to Voyager.

00:40:03.167 --> 00:40:04.293
I'm under attack.

00:40:04.368 --> 00:40:05.995
Give him some help, Mr. Tuvok.

00:40:17.014 --> 00:40:18.538
What have you done?

00:40:18.616 --> 00:40:20.948
We had to get you out of there
before we closed the barrier.

00:40:21.085 --> 00:40:23.451
You can't do that.

00:40:24.789 --> 00:40:26.188
Sit back and enjoy the ride.

00:40:26.257 --> 00:40:27.383
Paris to Voyager.

00:40:27.458 --> 00:40:28.652
I've got them.

00:40:28.726 --> 00:40:29.954
Find the deflector.

00:40:30.027 --> 00:40:33.519
I'm getting a lock on it now.

00:40:34.598 --> 00:40:37.192
My transporters are off-line.

00:40:37.268 --> 00:40:39.463
You better get
out of there, Tom.

00:40:39.537 --> 00:40:41.164
Not yet. I've got an idea.

00:40:41.238 --> 00:40:44.833
I am sorry to inform you,
Mr. Paris, but you have failed

00:40:44.909 --> 00:40:45.876
this examination.

00:40:45.943 --> 00:40:46.967
You will no longer

00:40:47.044 --> 00:40:48.636
be allowed to operate a vessel

00:40:48.712 --> 00:40:49.906
within Ledosian space.

00:40:49.980 --> 00:40:52.847
Something tells me that's
not going to be a problem.

00:41:20.010 --> 00:41:22.103
This is a beautiful blanket.

00:41:22.179 --> 00:41:24.044
Take it if you like.

00:41:24.114 --> 00:41:25.604
I don't need it.

00:41:25.683 --> 00:41:27.947
If environmental
systems ever go down,

00:41:28.018 --> 00:41:29.645
you might get cold.

00:41:32.022 --> 00:41:33.956
- I...
- You know...

00:41:34.024 --> 00:41:35.184
You first.

00:41:35.259 --> 00:41:36.453
Please, continue.

00:41:37.528 --> 00:41:41.794
In all the excitement,
I never apologized.

00:41:41.866 --> 00:41:43.197
For what?

00:41:43.267 --> 00:41:45.292
Causing you to miss
that conference.

00:41:47.371 --> 00:41:49.362
As a matter of fact, I...

00:41:49.440 --> 00:41:51.908
wanted to thank you for that.

00:41:51.976 --> 00:41:53.307
I thought you were angry.

00:41:53.377 --> 00:41:54.366
I was.

00:41:54.445 --> 00:41:55.707
But you were right...

00:41:55.779 --> 00:41:58.304
warp mechanics
can be studied anytime.

00:41:58.382 --> 00:42:00.816
The Ventu, on the other hand...

00:42:02.853 --> 00:42:04.787
Something's still bothering you.

00:42:07.658 --> 00:42:09.592
I'm concerned
for their well-being.

00:42:09.660 --> 00:42:11.787
They know how
to take care of themselves.

00:42:11.862 --> 00:42:13.090
That's not what I mean.

00:42:13.163 --> 00:42:16.291
Members of the Ledosian
expedition had the opportunity

00:42:16.367 --> 00:42:18.335
to scan my deflector
modifications.

00:42:18.402 --> 00:42:21.667
In time, they may find a way
to duplicate our technology

00:42:21.739 --> 00:42:23.673
and remove the barrier
themselves.

00:42:23.741 --> 00:42:26.107
I suppose it's possible.

00:42:26.176 --> 00:42:29.942
If I had never made
those modifications...

00:42:30.014 --> 00:42:31.641
We might
still be stranded there.

00:42:34.919 --> 00:42:37.513
I don't know about you,

00:42:37.588 --> 00:42:39.954
but I'm glad to be back
on Voyager.

00:42:42.026 --> 00:42:44.153
As am I.
